# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored —
# .env.example is the only one of the two ever committed.
#
# This file is read two ways, both by design (see progress-tracker.md
# Architecture Decisions):
#   - Locally, by Deno scripts: `deno run --env-file=.env ...`
#   - Pushed to the deployed Edge Function's secret store:
#     `supabase secrets set --env-file=.env`
# Never reference these as VITE_-prefixed vars anywhere — Vite inlines any
# VITE_* var into the client bundle, which would ship a Gemini key inside
# the publicly-readable Chrome extension (invariant 2 / CLAUDE.md § Security
# rules explicitly forbids this).

# 3 rotating free-tier Gemini keys — callModel(payload) tries key 1, falls
# through to key 2 then key 3 on quota/failure, skip-and-logs the cycle if
# all three fail (progress-tracker.md Architecture Decisions). Launch swaps
# this for a single paid-tier key behind the same seam — no code change.
GEMINI_API_KEY_1=
GEMINI_API_KEY_2=
GEMINI_API_KEY_3=
